WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.240
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.960
Are your pots and pans
and aluminum foil toxic?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.320
Today we start by looking at the
DNA damage that may be caused

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.640
by certain uses of
aluminum cookware.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.640
Over the last decades, the toxicity
of aluminum for humans

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.720
has been heavily discussed and
is still not completely clarified.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.920
Those occupationally exposed
to aluminum in like smelter plants

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.760
suffer from oxidative stress, free
radicals, that can damage their DNA.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.080
But what about just using
aluminum cookware?

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.240
Articles like this, suggesting an
unrecognized public health risk,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:59.160
was limited to the developing world
where cookware is made in informal shops

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.960
by casting liquid aluminum melted
from a collection of scrap metal,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.320
including the likes of lead batteries,
which is how you can get

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:13.320
so much lead leaching into peoples' food.
But then this study was published

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.560
suggesting the aluminum
itself may be harmful.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.480
Most of our aluminum exposure comes
from processed junk that contains

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.960
aluminum-containing food additives,
including those within some processed

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.160
cheeses, baking powders, cake mixes,
frozen dough, and pancake mixes.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.400
But approximately 20% of the daily
intake of aluminum may come

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:39.280
from aluminum cooking utensils,
such as pans, pots, kettles, and trays.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.360
To see if this may be causing a problem,
they took blood from consumers

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.240
that used aluminum cookware
versus those that did not,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.640
and found that not only were the
aluminum users walking around

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.800
with twice the level of
aluminum in their blood,

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.040
but they had more free radical damage
of their body fats and proteins.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:02.440
And the total antioxidant capacity of
their bloodstream was compromised,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:07.400
so, no surprise, suffered
significantly more DNA damage.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.080
And indeed, those with the highest
levels of aluminum in their blood

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.680
tended to suffer significantly
more damage to their DNA.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:21.680
No surprise, since aluminum is
considered to be a pro-oxidant agent.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.800
These folks weren't just casually
using aluminum pots, though,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.400
but specifically using them daily
to cook and store acidic foods,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.880
like yogurt and tomato sauce, which
can leach out more aluminum.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.080
But even just a week using like camping
dishes, which tend to be aluminum

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.320
since it's so light, if you were
incorporating something acidic,

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:49.280
like marinating a fresh catch in
lemon juice, could greatly exceed

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.360
the tolerable weekly intake
guidelines, especially for children.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.280
Once in a while is not going to make much
of a difference, but this suggests that

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.840
you may not want to be cooking
in aluminum day-in and day-out.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.480
What about aluminum drinking bottles?

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.200
They're nice and light but children
drinking two cups of tea or juice

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.880
a day from them could exceed the
tolerable aluminum exposure limit.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.560
So out of an abundance of
caution, safety authorities,

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.480
like the German Federal Institute
for Risk Assessment,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.120
recommend that consumers avoid
the use of aluminum pots or dishes

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:32.760
for acidic or salted foodstuffs such
as apple sauce, rhubarb, tomato puree,

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:39.200
or salt herring to avoid any
unnecessary ingestion of aluminum.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.360
What about aluminum foil?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.160
It's a common culinary practice to
wrap food in aluminum foil and bake it.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.800
The concern is that this
could potentially present

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.960
a hazardous source of
aluminum in the human diet.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.920
When put to the test, yes, there
was leakage from the foil to the food,

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.760
but the amount was so small that it would
be more of an issue for small children

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.440
or those suffering from
diminished kidney function.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.360
What about just wrapping of food
in foil to store in the fridge?

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:19.160
Only marginal increases in aluminum
are seen, unless the food is in contact

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.400
with both the foil and, at the same
time, certain other types of metal,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.800
for example stainless steel,
which is largely iron.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.635
And so that sets up a battery and so can lead
to tremendous food aluminum concentrations.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.520
And finally, you know how there's
sometimes a glossy side

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:41.200
of aluminum foil and then a dull side?
Which would be worse?

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.440
Fish fillets were baked and grilled
both ways, wrapped in the glossy side

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:52.600
versus wrapped in the dull side, and
no significant difference was found.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.400
In our next story,

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.880
we look at the best type
of pots and pans to use.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.080
Stainless steel is an excellent option,

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:03.387
the metal chosen in applications where
safety and hygiene are considered

00:05:03.387 --> 00:05:05.360
to be of the utmost importance,
such as kitchenware.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.040
But what about studies showing
stainless steel can leach

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.400
nickel and chromium into
foods during cooking?

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.880
(That’s what keeps the iron in the
stainless steel unstained by rust.)

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.160
The leaching is really only
when they’re brand new.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.800
Metal leaching decreases with
sequential cooking cycles

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.760
and stabilizes after the
sixth time you cook with it.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.040
Under more common
day-to-day conditions,

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.560
the use of stainless-steel pots
is considered to be safe

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:37.920
even for most people who are
acutely sensitive to those metals.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.680
A little leaching metal can be a good
thing in the case of straight iron,

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.160
like a cast iron skillet, which
can have the beneficial effect

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.520
of helping to improve iron status,
helping to potentially reduce

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.440
the incidence of iron deficiency anemia

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.320
among reproductive age
women and children.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:01.680
The only caveat is that you don’t
want to be frying in cast iron.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.320
Frying isn’t healthy regardless,
but at hot temperatures

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:10.320
vegetable oil can react with
the iron to create trans fats.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.920
What about using nonstick pans?

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.080
Teflon, also known as
polytetrafluoroethylene,

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.840
is used as an inner coating
material in nonstick cookware.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.880
Teflon’s dark history was the subject
of a recent movie called Dark Waters,

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:28.480
starring Mark Ruffalo
and Anne Hathaway.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.960
Employees in DuPont’s Teflon division

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.440
started giving birth to
deformed babies before DuPont

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.760
“removed all female staff” from the unit.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:43.840
Of course, they buried it all, hiding
it from regulators and the public.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.800
Despite this significant
history of industry knowledge

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.480
about how toxic some of the
chemicals used to make Teflon were,

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.480
they were able to keep it all hidden.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:58.320
But eventually they were forced to
settle for over half a billion dollars

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.880
after one of the chemicals was linked
to kidney and testicular cancers,

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.920
pregnancy-induced hypertension,
ulcerative colitis, and high cholesterol.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:11.040
“At normal cooking temperatures,
[Teflon]-coated cookware releases

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:16.194
various gases and chemicals that
present mild to severe toxicity.”

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.440
You’ve heard of canaries in a coal mine?

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.840
They're more like canaries in the kitchen,

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:27.480
as cooking with Teflon cookware is well
known to kill pet birds in the house;

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:32.360
or Teflon coated heat lamp bulbs
wiping out half a chicken flock.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.520
“Apart from the gases released
during heating the cooking pans,

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.640
the coating itself starts
damaging after a certain period.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:43.920
It's normally advised to use slow heating
when cooking in Teflon-coated pans,”

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:47.360
but you can imagine how
consumers might ignore that.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.640
And some of the Teflon can start
chipping off if you’re not careful

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:56.312
and make its way into the food, though
the effects of ingestion are unknown.

00:07:56.312 --> 00:07:58.320
This is the only study I could
find looking at the potential

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.160
human health effects of cooking
with nonstick pots and pans,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.840
and the use of non-stick
cookware was associated with

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:09.120
about a 50 percent increased
risk of colorectal cancer.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.120
But that may be because
of what they were cooking.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.120
Non-stick cookware is used in
hazardous high-heat cooking methods,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.400
like broiling, frying, grilling,
or barbecuing, mainly for meat,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.000
poultry or fish, in which
carcinogenic heterocyclic amines

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.600
are formed from the animal protein.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.960
And then the animal fat can
produce another class of carcinogens

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.960
called polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.880
Though it’s possible it
was the Teflon itself,

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.080
which contains suspected carcinogens
like that C8 compound from the movie,

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.680
also known as PFOA,
perfluorooctanoic acid.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.240
“Due to toxicity concerns,
this chemical has been replaced

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:53.960
with other chemicals such as
GenX, but these new alternatives

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:58.000
are also suspected to
have similar toxicity.”

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:03.520
But we’ve already so contaminated the
Earth with it that we now can get it

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.240
prepackaged in food before it’s
even cooked, particularly in fish,

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.760
dairy products, and meat,
which is now the main source

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.360
of human exposure to
these toxic pollutants.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.680
Of those, seafood is the worst.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.920
In a study of diets from around the world,

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:25.080
fish and seafood were major contributors
of the perfluoroalkyl substances,

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:30.400
as expected, given that everything
eventually flows into the sea.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.920
Though the aquatic food chain
is the primary transfer mechanism

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.720
for these toxins into the human
diet, “food stored or prepared

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.360
in greaseproof packaging
materials,” like microwave popcorn,

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.680
may also be a source.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:48.040
And in 2019, Oral-B Glide
dental floss was tested.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.440
6 out of 18 dental floss products
they tested showed evidence

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.982
of Teflon-type compounds.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.640
So, did those who used
those kinds of floss

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.560
end up with higher levels
in their blood stream?

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.200
Yes, apparently so.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.520
Higher levels of
perfluorohexanesulfonic acid

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:07.360
were found in Oral-B Glide flossers.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.360
There’s lots of environmental
exposures in the modern world

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.840
we can’t avoid, but we
shouldn’t be making things worse

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.880
by adding it to consumer products.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.520
But hey, at least it gives
us some power to lower

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:23.360
our personal exposure to
these harmful chemicals.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:24.040
Finally today,

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:29.320
we look at the role that aluminum may
play in causing Alzheimer’s disease.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.320
The so-called
"aluminum hypothesis"

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.040
for the cause
of Alzheimer's disease

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:37.480
dates back to 1965,

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.520
when the inadvertent
injection of aluminum

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:41.240
into the brains of rabbits

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.120
caused neurological symptoms

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.440
along with what initially
looked like Alzheimer's disease

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.600
tangles in the brain.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.240
Then, in the 1970s,
it was first reported

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.360
that the aluminum content
of Alzheimer's brains

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.840
was higher than that
of control brains on autopsy.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.960
Following that, there was
a rash of fatal dementia cases

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.840
attributed to dialysis fluids

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.000
contaminated with aluminum.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.800
This trio of findings

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.040
led researchers
to suggest that aluminum,

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.320
the third most
abundant element on Earth

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:12.240
(after oxygen and silicon),

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.480
may play a role
in the development

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.800
of Alzheimer's disease.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.600
The first crack in the theory

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.200
was the realization that,
upon closer inspection,

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.480
the tangle-like changes
in rabbit brains

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.120
were not much like those

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.400
found in human
Alzheimer's disease after all.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.600
The changes in aluminum-induced
dialysis encephalopathy

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.760
were also dissimilar.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.400
Aluminum could certainly
be toxic to the brain,

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.760
but not necessarily in a way

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.280
that had anything to do
with Alzheimer's disease.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.200
And, subsequent autopsy studies
of Alzheimer's victims

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.240
did not consistently find
higher aluminum levels,

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:49.080
and even if they did,
elevations in brain aluminum

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.720
could be a consequence
rather than a cause

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.520
(reflecting
Alzheimer's disease damage

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.440
to the blood brain barrier).

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.040
The aluminum hypothesis
came under heavy fire

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.560
in the scientific community.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.120
Only later did we learn
that the most vocal critics

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.560
were secretly-paid
aluminum industry hacks.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:06.840
In hindsight,

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.360
that was probably unnecessary,

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.800
as the tide of evidence
eventually turned against

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.400
the role of aluminum.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.000
What convinced me

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.600
was a meta-analysis
that failed to find a connection

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.800
between regular antacid use
and Alzheimer's.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.480
Processed foods
contain a variety

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.320
of aluminum-containing
additives,

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.280
such as anti-caking agents
in pancake mix,

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.840
melting agents
in American cheese,

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.560
meat binders, gravy thickeners,

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.360
rising agents
in some baking powders,

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.640
and dye binders in candy.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.560
However,
over-the-counter antacids

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.680
are probably
the most important source

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:41.720
for human aluminum exposure
in terms of dose.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.760
In terms of the safety
of dietary aluminum,

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.760
the tolerable weekly intake

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.680
is 1 mg per healthy kilogram
of body weight.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:51.080
So, if you weigh
about 150 pounds (67.5 kg),

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.040
you shouldn't get more than,
like, 10 milligrams a day.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.920
One day of Maalox

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.480
can give you
38 hundred milligrams,

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.480
nearly 400 times
the daily safety limit,

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.560
and nowhere on the label
does it say

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.600
not to take
with acidic beverages,

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.200
such as fruit juice.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.240
Washing an antacid down
with orange juice

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.400
can increase
aluminum absorption eight-fold.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.840
The total aluminum intake

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.560
in drinking water
and processed foods

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.600
in most countries may only
be a few milligrams a day.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:22.640
But, some antacids can increase
daily aluminum consumption

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:24.640
by up to several grams,

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:27.040
a thousand-fold higher.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.160
And so, if antacid use

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.040
isn't related
to Alzheimer's risk,

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.880
then ingested aluminum

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.240
is unlikely to be a cause.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.800
Now, just because aluminum
doesn't cause Alzheimer's

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:41.120
doesn't mean aluminum intake
is necessarily benign.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.480
Those who cook with aluminum

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.120
and store acidic foods,

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.800
like yogurt and tomato,
in aluminum cookware

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.720
suffer significantly more
DNA damage,

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.120
leading some regulators
to recommend consumers

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.600
avoid the use
of aluminum pots or dishes

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.120
for acidic or salted foodstuffs.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.240
In my video on antiperspirants
and breast cancer,

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.040
I note how the FDA
and European safety authorities

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.840
specifically advise against

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:08.360
using aluminum antiperspirants
on damaged skin,

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:11.480
which may even include
avoiding them after shaving.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.960
As a "metalloestrogen,"

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.880
aluminum absorption may explain

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.880
why breast cancer may occur
as much as twenty years earlier

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.840
in women using antiperspirant
and shaving their armpits

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.040
more than three times a week.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.360
You can also avoid
high dietary sources

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.040
by choosing non-aluminum
baking powder for baking

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.120
and avoiding
processed cheese.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:36.480
Aluminum salts can give cheese
"desirable slicing properties,"

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.480
but that means a single
grilled cheese sandwich

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.880
can end up exceeding
the World Health Organization's

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.480
provisional tolerable
daily intake of aluminum

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.080
by as much as 400 percent.

